  <h2>Why We Champion the MP4 (H.264 + AAC) Universal Standard</h2>
  <p>
    While streaming platforms experiment with proprietary or emerging codecs such as WebM, VP9, and AV1, our platform purposefully standardizes on the <strong>MPEG-4 Part 14 (MP4)</strong> container pairing H.264 video with AAC audio.
  </p>
  <p>
    This deliberate architectural decision ensures that every video downloaded from our servers is <strong>100% plug-and-play compatible</strong> across virtually every consumer computing device manufactured over the past 15 years. Whether you transfer the file to an older iPad, plug a USB drive into a classroom projector or smart TV, play it inside an automobile media console, or import it into Adobe Premiere Pro, Final Cut Pro, or DaVinci Resolve, the file plays immediately without codec errors or missing audio tracks.
  </p>

