  <h2>Our Commitment to User Privacy: Ephemeral by Design</h2>
  <p>
    We operate under a strict <strong>Privacy-by-Design</strong> ethos. We believe that utilities should do their job without surveilling the people who use them:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No User Accounts Required:</strong> We do not require you to provide your email address, create a password, or link social media profiles. The tool is immediately accessible to anyone.</li>
    <li><strong>No Search or URL Logging:</strong> We do not store persistent databases of converted video links, search terms, or user browsing histories. Conversion metadata exists only in volatile memory during the active session.</li>
    <li><strong>15-Minute Ephemeral Storage:</strong> Temporary media files generated during conversion are stored in isolated directories and permanently expunged by our automated background cleaner daemon within 15 minutes of completion.</li>
    <li><strong>Modern Encryption Standards:</strong> All communication between your web browser and our servers is secured using modern TLS 1.3 / HTTPS encryption, protecting your activity from local network eavesdropping.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Copyright Compliance and Responsible Media Stewardship</h2>
  <p>
    We maintain the utmost respect for intellectual property rights and creative authorship. Our platform is engineered to support legitimate, permissible, and fair-use media preservation:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Creator Self-Recovery:</strong> Digital creators who have suffered workstation drive failures and need to download backup master copies of their own published YouTube channel libraries.</li>
    <li><strong>Public Domain &amp; Government Archives:</strong> Historical educational footage, NASA space broadcasts, and government proceedings that belong to the global public domain.</li>
    <li><strong>Creative Commons (CC-BY):</strong> Open educational resources, university lectures, and creative assets published under open licenses permitting offline redistribution and remixing.</li>
    <li><strong>Scholarly Fair Use:</strong> Educators, students, and investigative journalists extracting short reference clips for critique, classroom presentation, and analytical research under statutory fair-use protections.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <em>Important Policy Notice: Our platform does not circumvent digital rights management (DRM), does not facilitate access to paid subscription video on demand, and strictly blocks commercial piracy.</em>
  </p>

